From 9dadc2efd13a16bd60d4553cfdb2b5967c2e53fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:16:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(turning): part off toward the chuck, never by the
 stock overhang

Second read of PR #3472: a plane inside the model took its scrap side
from how far the stock ran past each model end. A model with its grip
stub (Z-84..0, plane Z-70) under a stock with a 0.1 mm front facing
allowance parted Z-70..-67, 3 mm into the part, and the verdict used the
same rule and stayed silent.

